A||||7||RedGTFieroKCMO||Anyone have instructions on how to wire fastback taillights?||||5||
Z||000000||RedGTFieroKCMO||12-09-2001||12:57 PM||||Please help, ;(<P>This car was an 85 GT converted to fastback and last night I noticed that the taillights do not work as they should. The amber turn signals are not wired up at all and the brake lights are really out of wack. The signals cause the brake lights to come on.<P>What is the CORRECT way to wire up a conversion????<P>Thanks in advance,<P>Sean<BR>KCMO||||reg||5
Z||000001||Joe Torma||12-09-2001||02:00 PM||||You have to run a wire from under the steering column to the brake lights.  I posted how to do this a while back.  Its a white wire I think.  Then use the stock wiring to run the turn signals only.<P>------------------<BR>Its never going to be finished...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig2_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex2004||12-09-2001||04:50 PM||||I did the fastback conv. on my 84 SE and rewired it.  I ran a completely new brake wire from the brake switch near the pedal (white wire) and on each of the bulb sockets i cut the brake/turn signal wire and spliced the new brake wire into that... on the old brake/turn signal wire i bought 4 new sockets for the amber turn signals and wired the existing wire to the correct wire on the new socket... do you kinda get what i'm saying.  It was kind of confusing at first...  I <B>think</B> i completely cut the brake wire at the switch and spliced it and ran it to the brake lights.  I'll go look to make sure.  But that is how i did mine and haven't had any problems since then... I also wired my PONTIAC lights in except i just wired those into the parking lights instead of ignition power.  Let me know if you have any questions!  Alex..<BR>my e-mail is  <A HREF="mailto:Abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com">Abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com</A>   I have to go to work tonight but i'll reply as soon as i can.||||reg||3
Z||000003||Alex2004||12-09-2001||05:07 PM||||Ok, i cut the <B>white</B> wire at the brake switch and spliced the new brake wire into the part of the cut wire that goes INTO the brake switch and just discard the old white wire and tape it up. before you splice in the new wire take a test light and test the white wire going into the brake switch and push the brake to make sure it's still getting power, and then turn on your hazzards, left, right turn signals...your test light should NOT flash. Then run your new brake wire to the engine compartment, i ran mine from under the dash under the shift console and the ecm console and out through the rear firewall...  You'll just have to work your way around things till you get to the tail lights. Leave about 2-3 inches of wire left on your old tail light sockets so you can make a good splice, i soldered all of mine.  You need to cut the yellow wire going into the socket for your left side tail lights. and cut the green wire on the right. Splice your brake wire into the yellow wire for left and the green wire for right going INTO the socket.  Then once you complete that.  Wire the existing yellow for left green for right wires into the correct wire on your new sockets (make sure it's single filament) and then you'll also have to run a ground, or just splice into some other ground wire.  And that should be it.  You might want to ad a fuseable link to your new brake wire for safety.  I did and it's hasn't blown.  I also installed a third brake light.  That should cover it.  If you have questions just email me  <A HREF="mailto:Abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com">Abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com</A>  This isn't that hard of a job you just have to be patient.  Hope that helps!<P>Alex...||||reg||4
Z||000004||RedGTFieroKCMO||12-09-2001||06:03 PM||||Thank you everyone for the tips. I took apart the taillights today to get a better look at what I need. I was surprised to find missing light sockets for the 4 turn signal lamps. Can you buy the sockets separately from the assembly????<P>1.) Only the left backup light works.<BR>2.) The outermost passenger side tail lamp will not light up unless you press the brake and it looks like the parking light. (Not at full brightness).  The innermost lamp then dims....it's a complete mess.<P>Thanks again!!!<P>Sean<BR>KCMO||||reg||7
Z||000005||Indiana_resto_guy||12-09-2001||06:23 PM||||Might have been a plus to have access to the donor car in order to use the harness that was in it.<BR>You have sort of a job in front of you if your new to wiring!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Alex2004||12-10-2001||11:32 AM||||You can buy the sockets for the tail lamp assembly at autozone or most any auto store. Or you could go to a junkyard and get some off of another Fiero.  For the amber turn signal's be sure to get 4 reverse lamp sockets because they are the same as the amber turn signal sockets.  Now about your outermost passenger light.  I'd check the bulb, it probably needs to be replaced.  And then the other light dimming.  Probably a wiring problem.  Your reverse light that is not working.  I'd also check the bulb again.  And if it's good then it's probably ANOTHER wiring problem.  Hope that helps.<P>Alex...||||reg||2
Z||000007||cadaver||12-11-2001||01:12 AM||||All the ones I have done I got the wiring harness with the fastback parts. Se if anyone has a diagram of the GT lights. This will help alot. I would have it but my dog ate my factory manual.||||reg||1
